  "statement": "Given a string `s` and a string array `dictionary`, return _the longest string in the dictionary that can be formed by deleting some of the given string characters_. If there is more than one possible result, return the longest word with the smallest lexicographical order. If there is no possible result, return the empty string.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"abpcplea\", dictionary = [\"ale\",\"apple\",\"monkey\",\"plea\"]\nOutput: \"apple\"\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"abpcplea\", dictionary = [\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]\nOutput: \"a\"\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= s.length <= 1000`\n*   `1 <= dictionary.length <= 1000`\n*   `1 <= dictionary[i].length <= 1000`\n*   `s` and `dictionary[i]` consist of lowercase English letters.",
